'''turbine-dynamometer''' (tėr′bin-dī-na̤-mom′e-tėr), ''n.'' In ''hydraulic engin.'', a modification of the Prony brake, which adapts that device for application to vertical shafts or to horizontally revolving wheels on vertical shafts. {{smaller|It is used more especially for testing the power delivered from turbines (whence the name). A spring-scale is used instead of a weight in applying the brake-band. Compare ''Prony’s dynamometer.''}}

'''Turbinella''' (tėr-bi-nel′ä̤), ''n.'' [NL. (Lamarck, 1799), < ''Turbo'' (''Turbin-'') + dim. term. ''-ella.'']

